  "body": "The hooks I wrote for HTML and Fetch are a bit broken for nonces. In short: `<script src='https://example.com/' nonce='abcde'>` should be allowed by `script-src 'nonce-abcde'`, even though `example.com` isn't whitelisted.\n\nChrome handles this by setting a flag on the outgoing request during script loading ([in `ScriptLoader.cpp`](https://blink.lc/chromium/tree/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/dom/ScriptLoader.cpp#n376)), which I suppose we could replicate in HTML's \"prepare a script\".\n\n@annevk: how do you feel about an \"Already passed CSP checks so please don't do more\" flag on Fetch's `request`?\n",
